<title>UK: BOE gives money mkt 437 mln stg help at set rates.</title>
<headline>BOE gives money mkt 437 mln stg help at set rates.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said that it provided the UK money market with 437 million stg of assistance at established interest rates.  </p>
<p>			    EARLY	1100 GMT   1300 GMT   LATE</p>
<p> FORECAST SHORTAGE    1,600 MLN  1,600 MLN  =	    =</p>
<p> CUMULATIVE SUPPLY    =	    437 MLN    =	    =</p>
<p> DETAILS</p>
<p> BAND 1  BANK BILLS   =	    80 MLN*    =	    =</p>
<p>* INTEREST RATE - 5-11/16 PCT (INDICATES UNCHANGED BASE RATES)</p>
<p>! INCLUDES 357 MLN STG REPO EXPIRING OCTOBER 16, 17 and 18 AT</p>
<p>5-23/32 PCT</p>
<p>(INDICATES UNCHANGED BASE RATES)</p>
</text>
